# Keep the fixed programme title and make the live choreography explicit.
updates.update({
's1':dict(title='Trade. Guard.\nHunt. Claim.',content='Build Agents That Do It All.'),
's13':dict(layout=None,title='Watch the flow first.',content=[['One recipe','Choose Rebalancer or Guardian.\nInputs → decision → evidence.'],['One walkthrough','I show the controls first.\nWe run it together after the QR.']],label='WATCH FIRST · 18–20 MIN',notes=cue('Deck → embedded walkthrough → back to slides','Click Run Rebalancer or Run Guardian. Point to the numbered steps without running ahead. Return to slide 15 for the builder QR. An AEX app tour is optional only if the coordinator has accepted the full launch/output/cost/stop path.','First I will show you the route. Then we will run it together.','Everyone sees where the run, change, evidence and save controls are.','Use the browser lesson; no terminal setup is required.')),
's14':dict(title='Scan. Open. Follow along.',content=[['1 · Open the guide','Scan Build QR. Choose a recipe.\nKeep the page open.'],['2 · Follow with me','We run the first example together.\nYour own experiment comes next.']],label='JOIN THE GUIDED BUILD · 20–23 MIN',notes=cue('Builder QR → optional funding QR → back to Build QR','At 20:00 show Build QR. Everyone opens build.html. At about 21:00, if funding is configured, open the 15-minute operator window and show Funding QR briefly. Return to Build QR. A window opened at 21:00 closes at 36:00. People can register in parallel; it does not block the lesson.','Open this guide now and follow my first run. After minute 34 you will make your own change.','Builder QR and funding QR have distinct labels. Neither scanning nor showing a QR opens intake.','Skip the funding detour if the allowance is not ready; everyone can do the read-only build.')),
's15':dict(title='We build this one together.',kind='two',content=[['Rebalancer','Live Sui price + sample allocation.\nClick through with the presenter.'],['Guardian','Lending scenarios + capped response.\nSame follow-along structure.']],label='FOLLOW WITH ME · 23–24 MIN',notes=cue('Deck → Run Rebalancer (default) or Run Guardian','Take a quick show of hands if needed. Click the chosen Run button to open the embedded walkthrough. Lead ONE recipe, not both. Participants can follow it or choose the other card. Leave the walkthrough open for the next ten minutes.','Keep your guide open and click each step with me.','The presenter is in the embedded demo; the room is on the same builder page.','Default to Rebalancer; use Guardian scenarios if live reads fail.')),
's16':dict(title='Click Run. Inspect the result.',kind='two',content=[['Read → decide','Run the baseline in the walkthrough.\nIdentify the inputs and proposal.'],['Explain the boundary','Rebalancer: live price, sample holdings.\nGuardian: labelled risk scenarios.']],label='EMBEDDED WALKTHROUGH · 24–27 MIN',notes=cue('Embedded walkthrough step 1 → result','Click the baseline Run control. Read the summary, then expand the raw output if useful. Rebalancer: price, checkpoint, target and proposed change. Guardian: health factor, cap and whether it restores the target. No terminal typing.','A proposal is something we can inspect before granting action authority.','An actual browser execution result. No swap or repayment is claimed.','If the read fails, show the error and retry once or use Guardian.')),
's17':dict(title='Change one rule. Compare.',kind='two',content=[['Rebalancer','Click the 70% target step.\nCompare it with the first run.'],['Guardian','Click healthy, then unknown data.\nCompare the response and stop.']],label='EMBEDDED WALKTHROUGH · 27–31 MIN',drills=[],icons=[],arrows=False,notes=cue('Walkthrough change/compare → evidence','Use the next-step buttons to run the changed setting. Compare the saved baseline and new result. For Guardian, run the unknown-data case too. Then open the real Sui evidence link. Match the digest/status/balances/gas to the explorer; the historical Guardian receipt is a previous demo.','The rule changes a proposal. A chain receipt proves a separate executed action.','Both outputs remain visible for comparison. Unknown data stops Guardian.','Stay on the labelled scenario or previous receipt if the network fails; never fabricate a new transaction.')),
's18':dict(title='Save our example. End the run.',content=[['Keep the comparison','Save the inputs, change and outputs.\nKeep the evidence link.'],['Know the cost','Read-only lesson: no transaction fee.\nEach run finishes on its own.']],label='SAVE → DONE · 31–34 MIN',notes=cue('Walkthrough save step → back to slide 20','Click Save to download the comparison. Each run is one-shot. Explain that the optional coding-agent wrapper can have its normal model cost; this browser helper makes no model or signing call. Close the walkthrough and show Your turn.','That was our shared example. Now you will make your own change.','Saved evidence and a clear handoff to independent work.','If no successful result exists, save the error and next diagnostic step without calling it a success.')),
's19':dict(title='Now make it yours.',content='Your own recipe. Your own change.\nRun it, compare it, explain it.',notes=cue('Independent-build QR → participant screens','At 34:00 clearly say the guided demonstration is over. Show Build QR again for anyone who missed it. People may restart the walkthrough, switch recipe, or use advanced controls to make their own change. If funding opened at 21:00 it closes at 36:00; the operator handles export separately.','You now have 17 minutes for your own experiment. Pick one change you can explain.','Everyone knows this is independent work, not another presenter demo.','Pair up or use Guardian scenarios if connectivity is poor.')),
's20':dict(title='Your experiment. Your evidence.',kind='two',content=[['Sui Rebalancer','Pick your own target or band.\nSave what changed in the decision.'],['Liquidation Guardian','Pick a scenario or risk target.\nExplain the cap and unknown-data stop.']],label='BUILD ON YOUR OWN · 35–46 MIN',notes=cue('Participant builder pages','Circulate rather than continue a second presentation. Builders can repeat the click-through or expand advanced controls. Optional local code/download is for people who want it; it is not required.','Try one small change, compare the output, and prepare a short explanation.','A chosen setting and an output the participant can explain.','Use the browser route or work in pairs. Full funded swaps/repayments are outside this lesson unless separately rehearsed.')),
})

base='https://holonym-foundation.github.io/basecamp-builder-lab/'
qr=base64.b64encode((ROOT/'assets/build-qr.png').read_bytes()).decode()
js='''<script>(()=>{
const base=BASE,defs={build:['Choose your build ↗',base+'build.html'],library:['Starter sources ↗',base+'build.html#library'],guard:['Live Sui evidence ↗',base],hunt:['Non-chain Hunt ↗',base+'hunt.html'],receipt:['Previous pool receipt ↗',base+'?tx=Fvdxzog5tBYp3D4gg85PJxd6j4embkbcKyMKowhYnFV8'],guardian:['Previous Guardian demo ↗','https://suivision.xyz/txblock/4Fpevq1op4CiaQT79ZSvrQE8Jcc8reh8zvp5kjCPgiMG']};
const links={s12:['library'],s13:['build'],s14:['build'],s15:['build'],s16:['build'],s17:['receipt','guardian'],s18:['build'],s19:['build'],s20:['build'],s23:['library'],s25:['hunt'],s26:['build','hunt'],s29:['build'],s30:['build','guard']};
function protect(a){a.target='_blank';a.rel='noopener noreferrer';for(const type of ['click','keydown'])a.addEventListener(type,e=>e.stopPropagation());}
for(const [id,keys]of Object.entries(links)){const nav=document.createElement('nav');nav.className='workshop-actions';nav.setAttribute('aria-label','Workshop links');for(const key of keys){const a=document.createElement('a');a.className='workshop-link';a.textContent=defs[key][0];a.href=defs[key][1];protect(a);nav.append(a);}document.querySelector('#slide-'+id).append(nav);}
for(const id of ['s14','s19']){const box=document.createElement('div');box.className='workshop-qr';const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=base+'build.html';protect(a);const img=document.createElement('img');img.src='data:image/png;base64,QR';img.alt='Scan to choose Rebalancer or Guardian';a.append(img,document.createTextNode('Choose your build'));const p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent='Local code + browser lesson';box.append(a,p);document.querySelector('#slide-'+id).append(box);}
})();</script>'''.replace('BASE',json.dumps(base)).replace('QR',qr)
funding_config = ROOT/'funding-registration.json'
if funding_config.exists():
    registration = json.loads(funding_config.read_text())
    funding_qr = base64.b64encode((ROOT/'assets/funding-qr.png').read_bytes()).decode()
    js += '''<script>(()=>{
const form=FORM, fundingQR='data:image/png;base64,FUNDING_IMAGE';
for(const id of ['s14','s19']){
 const slide=document.querySelector('#slide-'+id),box=slide.querySelector('.workshop-qr'),a=box.querySelector('a'),img=box.querySelector('img'),p=box.querySelector('p');
 const buildURL=a.href,buildQR=img.src;
 const controls=document.createElement('div');controls.style.cssText='display:flex;gap:12px;justify-content:center;margin-top:18px';
 for(const mode of ['Build QR','Funding QR']){
  const b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='workshop-link secondary';b.style.cssText='font-size:21px;padding:10px 16px;cursor:pointer';b.textContent=mode;b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(mode==='Build QR'));
  for(const type of ['click','keydown'])b.addEventListener(type,e=>e.stopPropagation());
  b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const funding=mode==='Funding QR';a.href=funding?form:buildURL;img.src=funding?fundingQR:buildQR;img.alt=funding?'Scan to request workshop funding':'Scan to choose Rebalancer or Guardian';a.lastChild.textContent=funding?'Workshop funding':'Choose your build';p.textContent=funding?'15-minute window · 30 funded places':'Local code + browser lesson';controls.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b)));});controls.append(b);
 }
 box.append(controls);
}
})();</script>'''.replace('FORM',json.dumps(registration['url'])).replace('FUNDING_IMAGE',funding_qr)
js += '<script>' + (ROOT/'deck/demo-overlay.js').read_text() + '</script>'
for name in ['index.html','aex-v4.html']:
    path=ROOT/'deck'/name;p=path.read_text()
    match=re.search(r'window.SLIDES\s*=\s*(\[.*?\]);',p,re.S);slides=json.loads(match[1])
    for s in slides:
        if s['id'] in updates:s.update(updates[s['id']])
    # Same participant route in both variants; AEX tour remains an optional presenter cue.
    p=p[:match.start(1)]+json.dumps(slides,ensure_ascii=False)+p[match.end(1):]
    start=p.find('<script>(()=>{\nconst base=')
    if start!=-1:p=p[:start]+js+'</body></html>\n'
    p=p.replace('grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:42px','grid-template-columns:1fr!important;gap:42px')
    if 'hashchange' not in p:
        p=p.replace('fit(); go(start, false);', "fit(); go(start, false);\naddEventListener('hashchange', () => { const i = fromHash(); if (i >= 0) { if (drill.open) closeDrill(); go(i, false); } });")
    p=re.sub(r'<title>.*?</title>','<title>Trade. Guard. Hunt. Claim. Build Agents That Do It All.</title>',p,flags=re.S)
    if '#slide-s19 .h{bottom:430px}' not in p:
        p=p.replace('#slide-s14 .card h3{font-size:46px}', '#slide-s19 .h{bottom:430px}#slide-s14 .card h3{font-size:46px}')
    p=p.replace('</head>','<style>#slide-s19 .h{bottom:430px}#slide-s14 .card h3{font-size:46px}#slide-s14 .card p{font-size:30px}#slide-s16 pre,#slide-s29 pre{font-size:34px}#slide-s12 .cols,#slide-s17 .cols,#slide-s20 .cols{bottom:265px}</style></head>') if '#slide-s14 .card h3' not in p else p
    path.write_text(p)
# Presenter guide is generated from the same slide cues; it cannot silently drift.
intro='''<h1>Trade. Guard. Hunt. Claim.</h1><p>Build Agents That Do It All.</p><p>Private presenter guide · October 7, 12:30–13:30 SGT · 60 attendees · laptop-first</p><nav><a href="index.html" target="deck">Audience deck</a> · <a href="../build.html" target="build">Builder guide</a> · <a href="../index.html" target="evidence">Live Sui lab</a> · <a href="../register.html" target="registration">Funding form</a> · <a href="https://sui-basecamp-funding.j94fv2pvjn.chatgpt.site/operator" target="operator">Operator controls</a></nav><section><h2>Before the room enters</h2><ol><li>Click through both embedded lessons once. No terminal is needed for the presentation. Keep the downloadable Node source as an optional backup. Test both QR links on a phone and venue Wi-Fi.</li><li>Keep this page on your private screen. The deck’s N key exposes notes in the audience window.</li><li>Rebalancer = live price + sample holdings. Guardian = labelled risk scenarios. Neither is a deployed AEX agent or a live trade.</li><li>Pre-open a real Sui transaction and matching explorer. A prior Guardian receipt is historical evidence. Only add a live swap/repay if that exact funded route passes rehearsal.</li><li>Funding: operator opens a real form for 15 minutes, up to 30 validated recipients then waitlist. Amount remains unset until measured. Check the real registration link before projecting its separate QR.</li><li>AEX runtime/session state stays with Studio. No venue resubmission from this update.</li></ol></section><section><h2>Keep the original 60-minute shape</h2><p>0–6 why agents · 6–11 deployment · 11–16 authority + budget · 16–20 agent tour · 20–34 guided build · 34–51 open build · 51–57 share · 57–60 close.</p><p>At 18: show the walkthrough controls without running ahead. At 20: show Build QR; everyone opens the guide. Around 21: optionally open funding intake and briefly show Funding QR, then return to Build QR. At 23: choose one recipe and open its embedded walkthrough. At 24: click the baseline Run together. At 27: click the change step and compare. At 30: inspect real Sui evidence. At 32: save. At 34: explicitly hand over to independent building. Funding opened at 21 closes at 36; the operator exports separately. At 51: invite two short shares.</p></section>'''
sections=[]
for s in slides:
    sections.append(f'<section id="{s["id"]}"><div class="time">{html.escape(s["time"])}</div><h2>{html.escape(s["title"])}</h2><a href="index.html#{s["id"]}" target="deck">Open slide {s["num"]} ↗</a><pre>{html.escape(s["notes"])}</pre></section>')
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Basecamp · presenter guide</title><style>body{background:#0b0b0d;color:#eee;font:18px/1.55 system-ui;margin:0}main{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px}section{padding:24px;border:1px solid #38383c;border-radius:16px;margin:24px 0}h1{font-size:48px}h2{font-size:28px}a,.time{color:#2ed0bd}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font:inherit;color:#bdbbb8}li{margin:14px 0}</style></head><body><main>'+intro+''.join(sections)+'</main></body></html>'
(ROOT/'deck/presenter.html').write_text(page)
(ROOT/'deck/presenter.txt').write_text('TRADE. GUARD. HUNT. CLAIM. BUILD AGENTS THAT DO IT ALL.\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join(f'{s["time"]} | {s["title"]}\n{s["notes"]}' for s in slides))
